    "result_text": "All 42 tests pass, including the 3 new Cp29 postcode tests. Build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional, region-validated `postcode` support for owners:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (4-digit `^[0-9]{4}$` pattern, not in `required`). Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response) both gain `postcode`, and MapStruct auto-maps it by name. The 4-digit format is enforced by Bean Validation, so a malformed value like `\"12\"` yields **400** before reaching the controller.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `postcode` field (`@Column(name = \"postcode\")`, no `@NotEmpty` so it stays optional) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added a nullable `postcode` column to the `owners` table (tests run on `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the DDL).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Added `validatePostcode(...)`: when a postcode is present, it derives the city's region via the existing `Localities.forCity(...)` table and checks the fixed inclusive ranges (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), rejecting out-of-range with **400**. A city with no known region (`UNKNOWN`) accepts any 4-digit postcode, and an absent postcode is skipped \u2014 keeping the create contract backward-compatible.\n\nThe stored postcode is returned on `GET` via the auto-mapped `OwnerDto`.",
